<title>USA: U.S. refinery copper stocks rose in Nov. - ABMS.</title>
<headline>U.S. refinery copper stocks rose in Nov. - ABMS.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Refined copper stocks held by U.S. refineries rose to 41,100 short tons at the end of November from 40,300 short tons in October, said the American Bureau of Metal Statistics.</p>
<p>Commodity Exchange Inc copper stocks were 38,500 short tons in the month, up from 30,800 short tons in October.</p>
<p>Combined refinery and Comex stocks rose to 79,600 short tons in November from 71,100 short tons in the previous month.</p>
<p>U.S. refined production rose to 680,700 short tons from an October tally of 651,000. U.S. crude output was 686,700 tons, up from 673,500 in October.</p>
<p>((-- New York Commodity Desk, 212 859-1640))</p>
